\cf2 The purpose of this application is to monitor groups of trades placed in bulk via the Trade Allocations services, and on completion of the last trade in the group, notify other applications via Kafka events.\
The 
\f0\b Trade Group Monitor
\f1\b0  service itself is an additional service with a Mongo database that saves Trade monitor Kafka messages, with APIs to query the status by group or individual trade allocationid, userid, trustaccountid, or transactionid. This can be used by other systems like Admin to check the status of a user\'92s trades without having to query the Trade allocations table. The Trade allocations database table has to manage trade requests and should not be available long term. The intention was always to delete successful or error status trades and only keep unallocated requests in the database until they finish processing.\
Trade Monitor saves all the trade monitor request messages with the same data as found in the TradeAllocations table. As the trade monitor sends updated states, the Trade Monitor services will update the allocation status and data via its consumer.\
These trades will be saved into a MongoDB and APIs will be created to query the status of a group of trades.\

