\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 Trade Monitor:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 Kafka Stream aggregation to track allocations by group and notify when the whole group is done: 
\f1\b0 \
Trades are executed as a batch by using the TradeAllocations 
\f2\fs26\fsmilli13333 groupId
\f1\fs32  column. When a managed product investment is done, it consists of multiple trades that make up the investment according to the asset managers' specifications. E.g. Investing $100 in a product may result in 5 trades being placed with different weighting into different instruments. These trades will be placed by putting the instructions into the TradeAllocations (bulk trading) application\'92s database via its apis. It currently has a group ID which can be used to start the processing of the whole batch, as well as grouping trades together. We will be using this groupId to track trade execution and send out an event when the whole group has completed. Completed means when all trades was done, including failures\'85 ie. You could have a batch of 10 trades where 9 will pass and 1 failed and the Trade Monitor will send out an event to notify that it has completed.\
Create a new table that keeps track of the whole group with api methods to query the status of a group.\
This will be updated by the Aggregation message and if a Trade complete event is sent, all subsequent messages in the aggregator should be ignored. We can add duplicate checks in the consumer to ensure we don\'92t process a message twice. (Research on how to do this in Kafka streams methods and wether we can use our custom annotation should be done). This can happen on messages being re-processed incorrectly and duplicate error occur that will send error status updates.\
In order to notify the rest of the business when a batch of trades, bound together with the same GroupID in the TradeAllocations table, has completed, we will use the messages from the trade_request_monitor topic ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://purplegroup3.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/PG/pages/3030188057/Trade+Allocations+-+New+Kafka+implementation"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 see Trade Allocations documentation}}) and apply kafka stream aggregation to them.\
A new aggregated topic will be created called 
\f0\b trade_allocation_group_complete. 
\f1\b0 \
This topic will ingest TradeMonitorMessage events and create the following 
\f0\b KTABLE
\f1\b0 , aggregated by groupID.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa425\partightenfactor0

